    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39898" root="نصح" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِصَاحٌ</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>Thread</i> (S, K) <i>with which one sews:</i>
(S:) pl, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُصُحٌ</span> (K, TA; in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُصْحٌ</span>;) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِصَاحَةٌ</span>: (K:) the kesreh and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ا</span> in the latter are
not those which are in the sing., and the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span> is
added as a fem. sign of the pl. (TA.) [See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيْطٌ</span>.]

